{
  "draft": 1,
  "name": "did-auth-server",
  "description": "DID Auth, server side: recomputes the MAC from its own private key and compares it with the client MAC. Learning example, public demo keys.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "in",
      "type": "workflow-input",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "prv",
          "dataType": "bytes",
          "name": "Server Private Key",
          "defaultValue": "a4b87f7821ada85b4e7f63618924b4c3f3bbb78cddcab485a7ee6f15fdfc7261",
          "constraint": {
            "lengths": [
              32
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "cpub",
          "dataType": "bytes",
          "name": "Client Public Key",
          "defaultValue": "0415dc193b8e2a688d603303e85ec8fcc15dcba44ef2156a128c386b66b4f5e1d2188e7ca9d0385c02e72c6899f2771e86bb017a2d2903d89a2892c2199aec8f4d",
          "constraint": {
            "lengths": [
              65
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "nonce",
          "dataType": "bytes",
          "name": "Nonce",
          "defaultValue": "000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f",
          "constraint": {
            "lengths": [
              32
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "rmac",
          "dataType": "bytes",
          "name": "Received MAC",
          "defaultValue": "39b415c1dfeb8f52",
          "constraint": {
            "lengths": [
              8
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": "# Server inputs\nThe nonce is the one the server issued. `Received MAC` defaults to the client workflow output for the default demo values. Change one bit to see `false`.\n\n> Learning example that explains the protocol. Do not use it in a real service. The keys are public demo keys."
    },
    {
      "id": "ecdh",
      "type": "asymmetric-ecc-ecdh",
      "label": "ECDH",
      "props": {
        "curve": "p256",
        "format": "raw_x"
      },
      "note": "# 1. Shared secret\n`secret = ECDH(prvServer, pubClient)`\n- P-256, output format `raw_x`: the 32-byte X coordinate (the DIDAuth text does not name the format, this is an assumption)\n- Public keys are uncompressed 65-byte points (assumption)"
    },
    {
      "id": "sha",
      "type": "hash-digest",
      "label": "SHA-256",
      "props": {
        "algorithm": "SHA-256"
      },
      "note": "# 2. Hash\n`hash = SHA2-256(secret)`"
    },
    {
      "id": "ks",
      "type": "utility-slicer",
      "label": "Key",
      "props": {
        "offset": 0,
        "length": "16"
      },
      "note": "# 2. Key\n`key = hash[0,16]`: the left 16 bytes (AES-128 key)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ivs",
      "type": "utility-slicer",
      "label": "IV",
      "props": {
        "offset": 16,
        "length": "16"
      },
      "note": "# 2. IV\n`iv = hash[16,16]`: the right 16 bytes"
    },
    {
      "id": "cbc",
      "type": "symmetric-aes-encrypt",
      "label": "AES-128-CBC",
      "props": {
        "mode": "CBC",
        "padding": "None"
      },
      "note": "# 3. full_mac\n`full_mac = AES_ENC_CBC(key, nonce, iv)`\n- The 32-byte nonce is exactly two blocks, so no padding."
    },
    {
      "id": "cut",
      "type": "utility-slicer",
      "label": "MAC",
      "props": {
        "offset": -16,
        "length": "8"
      },
      "note": "# 3. mac\n`mac = full_mac[-16,8]`: the first 8 bytes of the last block (offset 16 bytes back from the end, length 8)."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmp",
      "type": "utility-compare",
      "label": "MAC matches",
      "props": {
        "operator": "=="
      },
      "note": "# Verify\nCompares the recomputed mac with the client mac. Not constant time: acceptable for a learning example, use `ct_equals` in a script for a real comparison."
    },
    {
      "id": "out",
      "type": "workflow-output",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "ok",
          "dataType": "bool",
          "name": "Verified"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "in.prv",
      "to": "ecdh.privateKey"
    },
    {
      "from": "in.cpub",
      "to": "ecdh.peerPublicKey"
    },
    {
      "from": "ecdh.sharedSecret",
      "to": "sha.data"
    },
    {
      "from": "sha.digest",
      "to": "ks.data"
    },
    {
      "from": "sha.digest",
      "to": "ivs.data"
    },
    {
      "from": "ks.sliced",
      "to": "cbc.key"
    },
    {
      "from": "ivs.sliced",
      "to": "cbc.iv"
    },
    {
      "from": "in.nonce",
      "to": "cbc.plaintext"
    },
    {
      "from": "cbc.ciphertext",
      "to": "cut.data"
    },
    {
      "from": "cut.sliced",
      "to": "cmp.a"
    },
    {
      "from": "in.rmac",
      "to": "cmp.b"
    },
    {
      "from": "cmp.result",
      "to": "out.ok"
    }
  ]
}
